---
import { DEMO_RECORDED_ON, demoKeyless } from "../../../data/demo-evidence.ts";
import { demoGate, NEAR_RPC_DEFAULT } from "../../../data/docs.ts";
import { site } from "../../../data/site.ts";
import type { CodeLine, CodeTab } from "../../ui/code-types.ts";
import CodeBlock from "../../ui/CodeBlock.astro";

/**
 * Quickstart. Prerequisites and build steps are those of docs/GUIDE.md "What you need" and "Build the
 * CLI" (Linux or Ubuntu WSL2, Rust 1.99.1 from rust-toolchain.toml, Foundry 1.8.6, solc 0.8.38 from
 * contracts/foundry.toml). The Ubuntu package list is README.md "Local quickstart". The audit flags
 * are from `crates/cli/src/main.rs:95-122`; its defaults point at the final gate, so the demo gate
 * needs both --deployment and --manifest.
 */
const directory = site.repoUrl === null ? "constitution" : (site.repoUrl.split("/").pop() ?? "constitution");
const clone: CodeLine[] =
  site.repoUrl === null
    ? [
        {
          note: "Clone the project repository with its submodules: git clone --recurse-submodules <repository URL>",
        },
      ]
    : [{ cmd: `git clone --recurse-submodules ${site.repoUrl}.git` }];

const prerequisites: CodeTab[] = [
  {
    id: "ubuntu",
    label: "Ubuntu",
    lines: [
      { note: "System packages. Needs an administrator account." },
      { cmd: "sudo apt-get update" },
      {
        cmd: "sudo apt-get install -y build-essential pkg-config libssl-dev ca-certificates git curl make python3",
      },
      { note: "Toolchains, as the user who will build." },
      {
        cmd: "curl --proto '=https' --tlsv1.2 -sSf https://sh.rustup.rs | sh -s -- -y --default-toolchain none",
      },
      { cmd: 'export PATH="$HOME/.cargo/bin:$HOME/.foundry/bin:$PATH"' },
      { cmd: "curl -L https://foundry.paradigm.xyz | bash" },
      { cmd: "foundryup --install 1.8.6" },
    ],
  },
];

const build: CodeTab[] = [
  {
    id: "build",
    label: "Build",
    lines: [
      ...clone,
      { cmd: `cd ${directory}` },
      { cmd: 'source "$HOME/.cargo/env"' },
      { cmd: 'export PATH="$HOME/.foundry/bin:$PATH"' },
      { cmd: "cargo build --locked --release -p constitution-cli" },
      { note: "Puts the binary on PATH for this shell." },
      { cmd: 'export PATH="$PWD/target/release:$PATH"' },
      { note: "Builds the local executor artifact that the audit needs." },
      { cmd: "forge build --root contracts" },
      { note: "Prints the headless subcommands." },
      { cmd: "constitution --help" },
    ],
  },
];

const audit: CodeTab[] = [
  {
    id: "audit",
    label: "Audit",
    lines: [
      { note: `Reads ${demoGate.account} and compares it with the committed deployment record and rules.` },
      {
        cmd: `constitution audit --deployment deployments/demo.json --manifest rules/demo/manifest.json --near-rpc ${site.nearRpc}`,
      },
    ],
  },
];
---

<div class="docs-prose">
  <p>
    You need Linux or Ubuntu on WSL2, not a native Windows shell: run Rust, Foundry and the NEAR
    tools inside WSL. These steps build the CLI and read public state. They do not need Docker, a
    wallet, an AI key or a signing key, and they send no transaction. Treat the commands on this
    page as instructions, not as evidence that a build or a run just happened.
  </p>

  <h3>Before you build</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Git, GNU Make and Rustup. The repository pins <strong>Rust 1.99.1</strong> in <code>rust-toolchain.toml</code> and installs it on the first Cargo run.</li>
    <li>
      Foundry <strong>1.8.6</strong>, which provides <code>forge</code>, <code>cast</code> and {" "}
      <code>anvil</code>. <code>contracts/foundry.toml</code> pins solc <strong>0.8.38</strong>, the
      Prague EVM and the optimizer at 200 runs.
    </li>
    <li>A C toolchain, <code>pkg-config</code> and the OpenSSL development headers.</li>
    <li>
      The repository checkout with its Solidity dependencies under <code>contracts/lib/</code>. If
      your checkout omits them, fetch the repository's pinned versions. Do not substitute newer ones.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <details class="docs-details">
    <summary>Install them on Ubuntu or WSL2</summary>
    <CodeBlock id="docs-prereq" label="Prerequisites" tabs={prerequisites} title="shell" />
  </details>

  <h3>Build the CLI</h3>
  <p>
    Run this from the repository root. The first build downloads the submodules and compiles every
    dependency, so it needs a network connection, disk space and time, and the machine has to stay
    awake. <code>forge build</code> produces the local executor artifact that <code>audit</code> reads.
  </p>
  <CodeBlock id="docs-build" label="Build" tabs={build} title={`${directory}/`} />
  <p class="muted">
    The binary is <code>constitution</code>. Everything after this build calls it by that name.
  </p>

  <h3>Audit the demo gate</h3>
  <p>
    <code>audit</code> reads the gate and the Base Sepolia proxy, then checks them against the
    deployment record and the committed rule set. It changes nothing. It exits 1 if any check fails,
    and a warning exits 0 without being a clean bill of health.
  </p>
  <CodeBlock id="docs-audit" label="Audit" tabs={audit} title={`${directory}/`} />
  <p class="muted">
    The CLI's built-in NEAR endpoint, <code>{NEAR_RPC_DEFAULT}</code>, may rate-limit (HTTP 429)
    under load. So every read on this page passes <code>--near-rpc {site.nearRpc}</code> {" "}
    explicitly, the endpoint this page itself reads through.
  </p>
  <p class="docs-note">
    <strong>Read every line, not only the exit code.</strong> The README recorded this audit on {" "}
    {DEMO_RECORDED_ON}: it failed only <code>gate_has_no_access_keys</code>, because the demo gate's
    access key was still present. That key was deleted on {demoKeyless.date}, and the identical
    audit then exited {demoKeyless.auditExitCode} with {demoKeyless.auditChecks} checks. State
    changes, so read every line of your own run instead of relying on these records.
  </p>

  <h3>What a write needs</h3>
  <p>
    Reading needs nothing. To send an upgrade through the demo gate you also need, and must be
    authorized to use:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      A funded <strong>NEAR testnet account</strong> and the <strong>path</strong> to its near-cli key
      file. The CLI reads the file; never paste its contents anywhere.
    </li>
    <li>
      A matching candidate implementation already <strong>deployed on Base Sepolia</strong>. The CLI
      does not deploy implementations.
    </li>
    <li>An available demo verifier, appraised against the compose hash its owner approved.</li>
  </ul>
  <p class="muted">
    Only the full local verifier integration also needs Docker, a NEAR sandbox, the gate wasm and the
    pinned verifier tool image. Account creation, funding, signing, deployment and paid inference
    each need the operator's authorization, and none of this page grants it.
  </p>

  <h3>Where to next</h3>
  <p>
    Run <code>constitution</code> with no arguments for the <a href="#tui">terminal UI</a>. To write
    an upgrade the rules accept, read <a href="#write-an-upgrade">the rules</a>. To run a ready-made
    attack without installing anything, open the <a href="/app">live demo</a>.
  </p>
</div>
